course: dictionary
lesson: 15669
title: The old word thrice
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Thrice is an old-fashioned word. It means three times. You will find it in old stories, fairy tales and poems. «The wizard waved his wand thrice, and the frog became a prince.» The wizard waved his wand three times, so thrice means three times.
explain: Today most people say «three times» instead of thrice. Thrice sounds formal and special, like something from a storybook. When you read it, picture the action happening again and again, counting to three.
explain: Look at the words around thrice to check your meaning. The sentence tells you what happened, and the word tells you how many times. Swap in «three times» to see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Thrice means three times.
fact: Thrice is old-fashioned and formal, so people today usually say «three times».
fact: You will meet thrice in old stories, fairy tales, poems and the Bible.
fact: In maths, thrice a number means that number multiplied by 3, so thrice 4 is 12.
fact: The pattern goes once, twice, thrice, then four times.
exercise: «The wizard waved his wand thrice.» What does thrice mean? | Twice | Once | *Three times | Four times
exercise: What is thrice 5? | *15 | 10 | 8 | 35
exercise: In the pattern once, twice, ___, four times, which word is missing? | Twice | *Thrice | Never | Once
test: «The dragon roared thrice, and the sky went dark.» How many times did the dragon roar? | Once | Four times | *Three times | Twice
test: Which is the modern way to say thrice? | *Three times | Quickly | Never | Often
exam: Mia says thrice means twice. Why is she wrong? | Thrice only means something in maths | Thrice means once | *Thrice means three times, and twice means two times | Thrice and twice are the same, so she is right
